  studio  and the data studio will make pass that  query to bigquery directly and fetch the  data  from bigquery using a native connection  the data does not pass through  apps script in any way so it results in  a much faster interaction  all the filters are automatically pushed  down and then the users also get a much  better  faster dashboard experience so finally  data studio passes that query into  bigquery which is the final query for  the dashboard which contains only the  data set  that this user is uh has access to c  and finally the results are back sent  back to data studio and  the history renders that data in  dashboard and the viewer finally can see  their dashboard with their own data so  since in the return query results step  only the users data set is passed there  is no way for  a different user to see that data set or  for this user to see data from a  different data set  so what's what does the end result look  like this is the whole process but when  the user finally opens the dashboard  they get a view that looks something  like this this is the view that all the  users  all the 1400 different partners see when  they open the dashboard they get a  dashboard like this  uh at the top there are filters they can  change the filters they can interact  with it and this dashboard will  indirectly present the data  for whatever filters or selections  they're making  each partner would see only their view  and not  they won't see anything else and based  on this dashboard  the team made some further improvements  where they added for their pages  they also added some monitoring where um  they could monitor  how the dashboard was being used through  strike stack driver  which partners were using it uh which  partners were uh  incurring additional uh data costs it's  also possible to set up  uh data limits by partner so  it's a future potential work is where we  could potentially take this  solution and then build in limits where  each partner would get a  say a certain amount of limit if they  hit that limit every month then  the dashboard won't become visible  another potential solution that can be  implemented on top of this is  using google analytics for data studio  it can be measured how the users are  interacting with the dashboard which  pages are they looking at  which pages where are they spending the  most time on  and then make the dashboard much better  and faster and more usable  for users that way if anyone wants to  build a similar  solution using data studio advanced  services and bigquery  uh this link with these links would be  helpful the first link  basically provides a step-by-step guide  on how to build a connector  similar to this and the second link  contains a code example of a similar  connector  you can just take the code example and  customize it to your own needs  so what finally happened after this  project this project was launched in  october 2019  after launch there were numerous  positive news stories over 200 new  stories were published on  digital trends and venture beats right  now over 6 000 users from more than 1400  partners  across the world are using this  dashboard every day  and as michael mentioned earlier uh the  connector that he created and the  dashboard the team  came up with it's working basically in a  no ops fashion  even with such high amount of usage and  there are over 30 000 accesses of the  datastore dashboard  and more than 800 000 queries have been  made in bigquery by all these partners  now waze uh this was a major  collaboration between waze and google  cloud  and waste plans to continue to promote  the data tools and build education  materials to  aid traffic planning across the world  and that brings us to the end of our  presentation  thank you
 

